cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  boardprobe: a hardware abstraction layer whose readings carry their
  provenance through to the result
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-11
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A uniform interface over an NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano's monotonic clock,
  die-temperature, rail-power and performance-counter sources, behind three
  backends -- live, recorded and simulated -- in which the provenance of every
  reading is carried in the value and propagated through every derivation as a
  lattice meet, so that a figure derived from simulated or recorded data cannot
  be labelled a measurement. Labelling passes through a single enforced choke
  point; an adversarial check attacks that invariant from fifteen directions
  and reports the outcome of each. Validation level 3, hardware-pending: the
  board was not reachable from the environment this package was built in, every
  declared sysfs path and counter name is unverified on hardware, and no figure
  in the repository was measured on the board. Research-grade; not
  flight-qualified, not certified and not approved for operational aerospace
  use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - hardware-in-the-loop
  - hardware-abstraction-layer
  - provenance
  - data-provenance
  - lattice
  - jetson-orin-nano
  - benchmark-harness
  - sysfs
  - perf-event-open
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/boardprobe"
